# App Check (issues #145, #718). Dev is provisioned to parity with staging/prod:
# its own reCAPTCHA Enterprise SCORE key (`salt-web-appcheck-dev`, allowedDomains
# s2-dev-eggman.web.app / .firebaseapp.com / localhost), registered as the App
# Check provider for this project's web app at tokenTtl 3600s, minValidScore 0.5.
# Public by design — a site key ships in the client bundle (see #715).
#
# Load-bearing: `enforceAppCheck` is a CODE constant that deploys to all three
# projects, so dev must mint real tokens or the first enforced deploy would 401
# every AI callable here. Do not empty this back out.
#
# The DEBUG TOKEN is deliberately NOT here — this file is committed, and a
# committed debug token is a standing attestation bypass. It belongs in an
# untracked `.env.dev.local` as VITE_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN, or a CI secret.
VITE_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_SITE_KEY=6Lf6GnctAAAAAMtFhj3-UQ8-nUh9mh_k1JrlzSqR
# PostHog (browser observability) — EU region, SAME project as staging/prod so the
# browser->CF->trigger trace chain is actually observable on dev (a core reason
# this env exists). An empty key makes the observability adapter a complete no-op.
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_qw73ZuXRSy6VBhZhVLRqaiNfVEB9kektGLSAGUyLTf5x
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false
# PWA install identity — dev is visually distinct from staging (amber) and prod
# (orange): violet theme + its own name for at-a-glance tab clarity. The theme
# colour and the icon variant both match this env's violet-600 TopBar
# (src/lib/environment.ts), so bar, chrome, and home-screen icon agree.
VITE_PWA_NAME=Salt (Dev)
VITE_PWA_SHORT_NAME=Salt Dev
VITE_PWA_THEME_COLOR="#7C3AED"
VITE_PWA_ICON_PATH=/icons/dev

# VAPID public key for web-push cook-timer notifications (issue #544). Public
# by design (the private key is a CF secret). Per-environment DISTINCT keypair — a
# subscription minted under one project's public key is undeliverable by another's
# private key. Empty disables the notifications toggle. Generate the pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys` and set the matching VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY secret
# + VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY env on the Cloud Functions side.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BBkDOWOLGf7v9hGsSfXWWB6Ds4l2z9cgBlGkJsGiuXiE6xyHTwPA14mp6bLZ28IJnLjQ-tRs9B0TrpEX-6OAHHQ
